  "parentCard": {
    "title": "The birthday card of fours",
    "minutes": 15,
    "includes": "cut-draw",
    "steps": [
      "Ask them what they love that you could find four of: four cars, four leaves, four socks. Hunt the four together around the house.",
      "Fold a paper in half to make a card, and help them draw all four on the front, counting out loud as each drawing lands: one, two, three, four.",
      "Let them cut little shapes or snips of colored paper and glue on exactly four to decorate.",
      "Stand the card up where the family eats and let them tell everyone what is on it and how many. If this is their birthday week, it is their own birthday card of fours."
    ],
    "notice": [
      "Do they land on four every time they count their drawings, even when they start from a different one?",
      "Do they check by recounting, or do they just remember it was four?",
      "Which do they enjoy more, the counting or the telling everyone after?"
    ]
  }
